# Supabase CLI local cache (gotrue-version, storage-version, etc.) --
# written by `supabase link`/`start`, not meant to be committed.
# Flagged in the security hardening handoff (2026-08-18); ungitignored
# until now.
supabase/.temp/

# Local scratch/reference files Claude drops in the repo folder while
# working — commit messages meant to be copy-pasted (not committed
# themselves), pentest reports, and the honeypot's real file-location
# notes (senseUS-honeypot-notes.md explicitly says this stays out of
# the repo, and it's referenced by name in commit_msg_078.txt-era
# history too). Ignoring these means a future `git add -A`/`git add .`
# can't accidentally sweep any of them into a commit -- important for
# the honeypot notes and pentest reports specifically, since the repo
# has been public since 2026-08-31. Added 2026-09-22 during a cleanup
# pass; nothing here was previously tracked except stray one-off
# commit_msg_*.txt files, which this also stops from recurring.
commit_msg_*.txt
Claude outputs/honeypot-locations.md
PENETRATION_TEST_ROUND*.md
